   "text": "The drawing shows Boc-protected, S-trityl-protected cysteine (Boc-Cys(Trt)-OH).\n\n- **Backbone:** a central CH carbon carries NH\u2013Boc, a CH2\u2013S\u2013Trt side chain, and a CO2H group.\n- **Protecting groups:** Boc is C(=O)OC(CH3)3 on the nitrogen, and Trt is triphenylmethyl, C(C6H5)3, on the sulfur.\n- **Stereochemistry:** only the CO2H bond is hashed, so it points away from the viewer and the implicit H points toward the viewer.\n  - Priorities are N > CH2S > CO2H > H. CH2S outranks CO2H because sulfur beats oxygen at the first point of difference.\n  - On screen, N (upper right) \u2192 CH2S (upper left) \u2192 CO2H (down) runs counterclockwise.\n  - Because H faces the viewer, the true sense is reversed to clockwise, so the centre is R. This is L-cysteine.\n- **SMILES chirality tag:** N[C@@H](CS)C(=O)O is the L-cysteine pattern, so I used @@ in the full SMILES.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)(C)OC(=O)N[C@@H](CSC(c1ccccc1)(c1ccccc1)c1ccccc1)C(=O)O"
